1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,040
Hell Pace! Hell Pace! Dream Safe!

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:08,740
Hell Pace !Hell Pace!

3
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:11,780
Hell Pace!

4
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:41,300
Give those back!

5
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:42,860
You'll pay for this!

6
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:49,050
AAMH!

7
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:50,740
HUM! HUM!

8
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:54,910
HUM!

9
00:01:54,993 --> 00:01:56,080
A-A-A-A-A!

10
00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:25,738
You're Sabo, right?

11
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:28,220
Huh? Wait a sec.

12
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:29,838
You're Joey Bonnie.

13
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:33,337
If you know who I am, then
that saves us some time.

14
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:35,185
I think we have the same goal.

15
00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:39,067
Intruders in the guard room!

16
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:41,697
They've stolen the keys
to the slave's colors!

17
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:42,900
Kill them on sight!

18
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:47,637
I knew Kuma had a
daughter, but that's all.

19
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:51,577
We've never met before, but I've been
keeping up with your group for a while.

20
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:57,040
Point is, I know you guys are my allies,
and I trust you to save my dad! We will.

21
00:02:57,380 --> 00:02:58,968
That's what we're here for.

22
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:05,040
Karasu! I'm here.

23
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:07,157
I found the keys.

24
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:09,217
Take them and tell the other captains.

25
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:13,700
Once you rescue Kuma and unlock the
slave callers, go straight back to HQ.

26
00:03:14,140 --> 00:03:15,905
Your mission will be complete.

27
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:18,837
We don't have much time.

28
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:19,960
Go, and hurry!

29
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:21,580
What about you, Sabo?

30
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:22,590
I'll be all right.

31
00:03:22,673 --> 00:03:24,477
I'll follow once I finish my business.

32
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:26,000
Got it. Be careful!

33
00:03:31,940 --> 00:03:33,717
I assume you'll be leaving soon.

34
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:34,630
What's next?

35
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:36,737
I'll be going straight to Egghead.

36
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:37,820
I'll by yourself?

37
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:38,910
Uh-huh.

38
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:40,657
You sure that's smart?

39
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:42,622
It's world government territory.

40
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:43,940
It doesn't matter!

41
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:46,572
I need Vegapunk to restore my dad's mind!

42
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:50,100
That's the whole reason
I went to see. Hold on.

43
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:53,257
Do you really think he can
get Kuma back to normal?

44
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:55,577
Well, I'm not leaving until he does it.

45
00:03:55,660 --> 00:03:58,100
So he'd better fix them, or else.

46
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:03,200
There they are! This way! Hurry!

47
00:04:13,140 --> 00:04:15,880
Where are they? Damn it. They're gone.

48
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:18,637
How strange.

49
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:20,661
I could have swore I saw someone.

50
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:22,510
Thanks.

51
00:04:22,593 --> 00:04:23,423
Nice timing.

52
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:27,900
Why do they insist on making
things so difficult for us?

53
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:32,777
There simply aren't enough guards in this
tower to patrol a space as large as this.

54
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:33,690
What?

55
00:04:33,773 --> 00:04:35,077
Surely you must have heard.

56
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:37,197
We're short on manpower because of...

57
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:38,760
you know what? Pardon?

58
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:42,940
Apparently they saw it. Saw what?

59
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,297
The lost chamber.

60
00:04:44,380 --> 00:04:46,037
Keep your voice down, you fool.

61
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:47,708
Don't even joke about that.

62
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:52,820
Thanks, Sabo. Well,

63
00:04:53,140 --> 00:04:57,217
Egghead is in the new world, so it looks
like we're headed in opposite directions.

64
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:59,180
Just be careful. Okay.

65
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:01,446
I'll keep you in my thoughts.

66
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:03,530
Huh?

67
00:05:03,613 --> 00:05:05,340
Thanks, but this is weird. Yeah?

68
00:05:06,020 --> 00:05:07,720
You're not a pirate like me.

69
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:11,988
Don't know how I feel about a
revolutionary treating me nice.

70
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:14,341
We both want to save Kuma, right?

71
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:16,050
Hmm.

72
00:05:16,133 --> 00:05:16,963
Get him back safe.

73
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:25,157
What do you wish to ask,
Cobra King of Alabasta?

74
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:26,220
Speak up!

75
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:30,640
Well, I suppose I should
start at the beginning.

76
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:35,260
It is said that roughly 800 years ago,

77
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:40,441
there were 20 monarchs who came together
to form the world government as we know it.

78
00:05:41,140 --> 00:05:45,920
After creating this new regime, they
relocated their families to Mariejois.

79
00:05:46,660 --> 00:05:50,137
Those families became known
as the Celestial Dragons,

80
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:52,691
and they have reigned for eight centuries.

81
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:55,440
But there was no supreme ruler.

82
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:58,120
They all shared their power equally.

83
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:02,541
The Empty Throne is a
monument to that commitment.

84
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:06,486
It symbolizes their promise to
never allow a dictator to reign.

85
00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:10,077
The twenty monarchs placed
their weapons at its feet,

86
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:12,620
vowing that none would sit upon it.

87
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:17,260
Meanwhile, in their homelands,
new royal families were selected.

88
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:20,522
And those families have
been in power ever since.

89
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:24,737
Therefore, their names all differ
from those of the first twenty.

90
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:28,100
A new line of succession
was born in each nation.

91
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:30,800
And yet Alabasta is different.

92
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:34,637
Queen Lily of the
Nefertari family was named

93
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:37,057
one of the first twenty
monarchs at the time.

94
00:06:37,140 --> 00:06:39,611
But she did not become a celestial dragon.

95
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:41,620
She returned to Alabasta.

96
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:45,600
And we, the Nefertari family,
still reign there to this day.

97
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:51,260
I assume that is the reason there are only
nineteen weapons surrounding the throne.

98
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:55,880
What you've said is correct,
but what is your point?

99
00:06:56,560 --> 00:07:00,207
Well, I've been perusing some
old books we have in my country.

100
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:04,557
Of course, none of those texts
predate the Void century,

101
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:06,297
so we cannot know the full truth.

102
00:07:06,380 --> 00:07:08,560
But I still notice something odd.

103
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:10,621
Lily is missing.

104
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:13,260
Her name is nowhere to be found.

105
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:20,320
It would seem she never made it
back to the Kingdom of Alabasta.

106
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:24,160
Her younger brother ruled
the country in her stead.

107
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:27,173
Nothing else about her fate was written.

108
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:30,069
Could you tell me what
you know about that?

109
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,480
Is that all you wish to ask?

110
00:07:33,780 --> 00:07:36,100
About an 800-year-old story?

111
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:37,820
As you said,

112
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:42,452
the monarch of the Nefertari family
did not choose to stay like the others.

113
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:46,200
But the belief was that she
returned to her country.

114
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:49,744
No one knows why she left
or where she ended up.

115
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:52,760
Those details have been lost to time.

116
00:07:53,980 --> 00:07:56,420
That is all we know, I'm afraid.

117
00:07:58,540 --> 00:08:00,320
Then what is the D?

118
00:08:01,780 --> 00:08:04,180
And why would you ask that?

119
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:09,060
It's quite brief, but there is a letter
that Queen Lily wrote 800 years ago.

120
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:13,540
Our family has passed it
down for generations now.

121
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:19,940
Ah! No!

122
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:21,160
Let it go!

123
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:22,400
I'm begging you!

124
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:23,680
Please stop!

125
00:08:23,960 --> 00:08:25,980
Don't do this! Please!

126
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:27,730
Please!

127
00:08:27,813 --> 00:08:28,643
You're hurting me!

128
00:08:28,726 --> 00:08:29,580
This isn't right!

129
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,160
Somebody stop him!

130
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:37,420
It was hard work, but I finally did it!

131
00:08:37,580 --> 00:08:39,500
I never gave up on my dream!

132
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:42,240
And now the giant mermaid belongs to me!

133
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:45,480
Good lad! She's all yours! The fine catch!

134
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:47,037
Please, someone help!

135
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:48,477
He's going to take me away!

136
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:49,736
This is a nightmare!

137
00:08:49,980 --> 00:08:51,900
Oh, my poor sweet Shirahoshi!

138
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:55,080
Oh, I wonder what I should feed her.

139
00:08:55,340 --> 00:08:57,497
I can't wait for her to
pick me up with her big,

140
00:08:57,580 --> 00:09:00,462
beautiful hands and carry
me around town all day.

141
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:03,980
Look at my new pet, Shirahoshi.

142
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:06,680
Now stop looking and get out of my way.

143
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:10,120
Everyone loves me.

144
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:16,920
And if you don't obey me, I'll be
sure to give you help. I refuse.

145
00:09:18,460 --> 00:09:20,037
Why won't anyone help?

146
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:22,020
Why are you just watching?

147
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:24,080
Please save me!

148
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:25,840
Why now?

149
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:28,937
My father and all our guards
are in the council tower.

150
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:30,360
He doesn't own me!

151
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:31,540
This isn't right!

152
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:35,560
It seems there's only one option.

153
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:38,020
You'll help me?

154
00:09:40,340 --> 00:09:41,820
Run away, hurry!

155
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:43,390
Oh, no!

156
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,640
You mermaid!

157
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,060
Are you being rebellious already?

158
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:48,917
I should have you flinch!

159
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,177
Honestly, it's rude of her
to expect us to bail her out!

160
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:53,500
She turned us down!

161
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:56,097
We can turn down saving
her from slavery, right?

162
00:09:56,180 --> 00:09:57,010
That's right!

163
00:09:57,093 --> 00:09:59,860
I won't put my neck on the
line for her! Make way!

164
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:03,637
You pathetic, filthy cowards
are as spineless as a jellyfish!

165
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:04,550
Ah!

166
00:10:04,633 --> 00:10:05,463
The princess!

167
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:06,790
Ah!

168
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:08,760
Oh, you can't fight!

169
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:10,959
They'll destroy your whole country!

170
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:15,677
Sister, forgive us for
letting this happen!

171
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:17,297
I'm so glad you're here!

172
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:20,480
I just wish we'd come
sooner, but you're safe now.

173
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:22,565
We'll set you free right away.

174
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:25,780
Let's return home.

175
00:10:25,940 --> 00:10:28,297
We'll never come to
this cursed place again.

176
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:29,792
Thank you for commotion.

177
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:31,517
Oh, you're going home?

178
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:33,417
That sounds like a splendid idea to me.

179
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:36,757
The mermaid stays as my pet,
and you get out of my hair.

180
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,428
I don't want any fish, men.

181
00:10:38,620 --> 00:10:39,500
You bastard!

182
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,460
Give her back!

183
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:43,842
How dare you treat her that way!

184
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:46,980
You pay for this! Yes!

185
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:51,180
Kill them, Kuma!

186
00:10:52,300 --> 00:10:54,340
My invincible space!

187
00:11:00,180 --> 00:11:01,860
Don't kill them, please!

188
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:04,290
Shirahoshi!

189
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:05,870
Rebecca!

190
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:07,817
We'll get those chains off of you!

191
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:08,730
Rebecca!

192
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:10,214
It's that creep again!

193
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:13,340
I don't care who he is, we'll stop him!

194
00:11:15,220 --> 00:11:18,977
Just checking you, Skyev, but I
can kick his ass this time, right?

195
00:11:19,060 --> 00:11:19,890
Of course!

196
00:11:19,973 --> 00:11:22,056
I'll take full responsibility for it!

197
00:11:24,180 --> 00:11:29,360
A pity that a former warlord has been
reduced to this, but I won't relent! Forward!

198
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:30,550
Let's go!

199
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:33,300
Ryuboshi! Mamboshi! Ready!

200
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:34,900
Just kill them, Kuma!

201
00:11:35,040 --> 00:11:35,920
It'll be fine!

202
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:40,117
Even if they are royalty, there's no
problem a little money can't solve.

203
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:41,717
They are just fish.

204
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:43,140
How dare you!

205
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:45,480
Please calm down!

206
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:47,602
You mustn't forget your royalty!

207
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:49,120
Don't stop me!

208
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:50,771
Leave it to them instead!

209
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:53,580
Our sister is in trouble!

210
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:55,020
I can't just watch!

211
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:58,117
Why do they have a right
to step up when we don't?

212
00:11:58,200 --> 00:11:59,671
Because they are pirates!

213
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:01,574
Think of your country!

214
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:02,954
You could start a war!

215
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:05,500
Damn you, Miosgaard!

216
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:08,637
Don't you dare think I forgot
the insult you dealt to me!

217
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:12,660
Come on, kill Mulescarp this instant!

218
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:21,820
Slug dragon calls me!

219
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:24,515
I'll show the techniques drill dragon!

220
00:12:25,140 --> 00:12:25,970
Sir Lee!

221
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:26,920
Sir Sly!

222
00:12:27,100 --> 00:12:28,180
Don't do it!

223
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:29,653
He'll put you to death!

224
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:31,940
Kill him!

225
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:33,900
And I fail!

226
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:42,140
Chalos!

227
00:12:44,140 --> 00:12:46,000
They killed him!

228
00:12:46,380 --> 00:12:48,100
Oh, the inhumanity!

229
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:49,640
This is murder!

230
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:52,800
The murder of a celestial dragon!

231
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:55,780
Someone call the admirals now!

232
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:10,500
Stop it, Kuma!

233
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:12,075
Please don't do this!

234
00:13:12,820 --> 00:13:14,880
We came here and I set you free!

235
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:16,330
Okay?

236
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:19,266
You don't have to follow
their orders anymore!

237
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:20,680
We can help you!

238
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:22,900
Let's go home together!

239
00:13:24,560 --> 00:13:26,660
What is a giant doing here?

240
00:13:27,580 --> 00:13:28,410
Morley!

241
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:31,580
I got the keys from Sabo! Come on!

242
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:33,760
What is that? An intruder!

243
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:36,897
That's Morley, a captain
of the Revolutionary Army!

244
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:39,240
Going down! See ya!

245
00:13:43,980 --> 00:13:45,260
Oh, my son!

246
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:47,168
What have they done to you?

247
00:14:02,080 --> 00:14:03,160
Great Emu!

248
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:05,200
King Cobra is still here!

249
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:08,300
Did he say Imu?

250
00:14:25,020 --> 00:14:25,850
Lily...

251
00:14:28,540 --> 00:14:30,920
No one is meant to sit upon that throne.

252
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:35,365
The world should not bend
to one person's will.

253
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:37,120
This was the oath.

254
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:40,160
There are two things
that I wish to tell you.

255
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:43,960
And one thing I wish to ask of you, Cobra.

256
00:14:44,660 --> 00:14:46,100
But who are you?

257
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:49,860
The name Emu sounds familiar.

258
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:52,180
Surely it's a coincidence.

259
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:55,097
But among the first twenty, there was...

260
00:14:55,180 --> 00:14:56,400
Cease your prying.

261
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:58,900
I will not respond to it.

262
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:02,860
But I shall answer your previous question.

263
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:09,520
The D you speak of is the name of
those who once opposed us long ago.

264
00:15:10,900 --> 00:15:14,900
It has reared its ugly head
rather frequently in recent years,

265
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:18,997
among hollow shells who don't even
know the meaning of their own name.

266
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:22,940
That wretched faction, like
